    "searchText": "Scenario 1 – Sales system \nYou are a newly qualified CA working on the audit of Premiux Furnishings Ltd (‘Premiux’). \nPremiux is a fast-growing company which sells a range of unique luxury home furnishings from \ntheir stores based throughout the UK. \nYou have been provided with the following information and have been asked to identify and \nevaluate key controls and design tests of control to verify whether the controls are operating \neffectively. \nCustomer orders \nOrders are placed by customers, primarily through the company’s online website. Once the \norder is submitted by the customer and payment is made, a unique sequentially numbered \nsales order will be created automatically in the sales system. One of the two sales managers \ncarries out regular sequence checks looking for duplicate or missing sales order numbers which \nwill be investigated if identified.  \nAny orders that are over £5,000 in total will be held as ‘pending awaiting approval’. There are no \naccess restrictions on who can approve these. Once approved, the system will keep a time log \nof the approval.  \nDespatches to customers \nOnce products have been picked by a member of the warehouse team, a GDN is created. The \nGDNs will be printed by the warehouse team and a check of the product descriptions and \nquantities between the sales order, GDN and physical goods will be made by a second member \nof the warehouse team prior to the despatch of goods. \nThe delivery of products is outsourced to a global courier company. Once delivered to \ncustomers, all orders must be signed for by the customer using a hand-held computer device. \nAt the end of each week, the courier company will send the warehouse team a report of each of \nthe customer deliveries made during the week and copies of the signatures received. This report \nis filed online with the GDN, however no check is made to match each delivery confirmation to \nits corresponding GDN to confirm that all deliveries have been completed.  \nCustomer invoices and payments \nOnce confirmation of receipt of goods is received, an invoice will be emailed to the customer. \nEach sales order will be marked as status ‘invoiced’ once the invoice has been emailed and this \nwill not allow any further invoices to be raised.  \nThe ERP system automatically matches the sales order, GDN, invoice and customer payment \nreceived at the time of the order using the sales order reference number. An exception report \nwill be generated automatically from the ERP system and any exceptions will be reviewed by the \naccounts receivable manager and corrective action taken as required.  \nAt the end of each month, a reconciliation is performed between the sales listing and the \ngeneral ledger by the finance team and reviewed by the finance manager. Any differences are \ninvestigated, and the finance manager signs the reconciliation to evidence their review.  \n \n \n",
